<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elizabeth Charlotte, Madame Palatine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1652–1722</span> · Also known as Liselotte von der Pfalz, Elizabeth Charlotte of the Palatinate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elizabeth Charlotte of the Palatinate, known as Liselotte, was a daughter of Elector Charles I Louis who married Philippe, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a>, brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>, in 1671. When her brother Charles II died without heirs in 1685, Louis XIV claimed Palatine lands in her name, a pretext for the Nine Years' War and the devastation of the Palatinate. She is also remembered for thousands of frank letters describing life at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elizabeth-charlotte-madame-palatine.jpg" alt="Elizabeth Charlotte, Madame Palatine" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: After Pierre Mignard I · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liselotte,_Duchess_of_Orl%C3%A9ans_in_1675_by_Mignard.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
